        "title": "Cost Accounting - The Cost Measurement Engine",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Cost accounting is the **internal measurement layer** (managerial side, no GAAP/IFRS rules)\nthat answers: *what does a unit actually cost, and how does total cost behave as volume\nchanges?* Every pricing, make-or-buy, keep-or-drop, and break-even decision rests on\nclassifying costs correctly. The master distinction is **cost behavior** (fixed vs variable)\nand **cost traceability** (direct vs indirect)."
    }
